    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233">

                <pb facs="0415" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg345"/>

                <head>Mr. Campbell to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New Orleans</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 12, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In my despatch No. 8, of December 31st, I
                    communicated information in reference to the seizure by Mexican authorities of
                    some twenty thousand dollars of specie from the American schooner Mary Bertrand,
                    wrecked on their coast near Bagdad.</p>
                <p>I have now the satisfaction of informing you that that specie has been restored
                    to its owners. This just end was not attained, however, without an expenditure
                    of several hundred dollars and a vexatious and damaging delay of two weeks.</p>
                <p>This information I receive from Captain McGaffey of the Mary Bertrand, who
                    arrived here last night.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LEWIS D. CAMPBELL.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
